@copilot Update this existing Lambda SQS PR directly to preserve the pre-existing shared-helper metric assertion pattern when extending `AwsLambdaSqsMessageHandlerTest.processSpans()`. The user now wants the new key-only metric guidance applied to new tests only, not retroactively to existing tests. This intentionally supersedes the earlier request on this PR to use key-only assertions, remove numeric/value checks, and leave shared assertion helpers untouched.

The original test called `AwsLambdaSqsMetricsAssertions.assertMetrics(testing, TracingSqsEventHandler.INSTRUMENTATION_NAME, "queue1", 3, 2, null)`. The current PR replaces that call with large inline key-only assertion blocks. Restore the helper-based pattern. Extend `instrumentation/aws-lambda/aws-lambda-events-2.2/testing/src/main/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/awslambdaevents/v2_2/AwsLambdaSqsMetricsAssertions.java` only as needed to express the split processing-duration points for the existing mixed-batch test in `instrumentation/aws-lambda/aws-lambda-events-3.11/library/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/awslambdaevents/v3_11/AwsLambdaSqsMessageHandlerTest.java`. Keep existing helper callers working without unrelated rewrites. The required expectations are 2 non-error processing-duration observations with no ERROR_TYPE, 1 failed processing-duration observation with ERROR_TYPE="_OTHER", and consumed-message counter value 2 with no ERROR_TYPE. Use the helper's existing exact attribute-value assertion style, including operation "process", system AWS_SQS, and destination "queue1". Preserve its existing count, positive-duration, unit/description, and exact emitted-metric inventory checks while accommodating the two duration points. The goal is a focused extension of existing assertions, not a migration to key-only assertions or a new test matrix.

Preserve all span and mixed-batch response assertions, the Boolean-response design, production behavior, exception handling, and all other tests. Do not reintroduce the previously removed suppression/helper-test matrix, change production code or documentation, touch other PRs, or merge/rebase branches. Update this PR's existing head branch, not a separate follow-up PR, and preserve its live base and draft/ready state. Follow repository formatting instructions and run the narrow relevant existing tests. Acceptance: `processSpans()` again delegates metric assertions through the existing shared helper pattern; the required success/error point attributes and counts and consumed-message value are asserted; no existing coverage is dropped; unnecessary inline key-only churn is removed. Do not reply to human comments, resolve threads, or request a review.

